Assess scope for change-card {{.key}}: "{{.title}}".

READ: Change-card description at {{.file_path}}

ASSESS: Is this properly scoped as a change-card or is it too large?

CHANGE-CARD = standalone, atomic, low-risk change. Examples: fix a label, update a config value, add a missing validation, tweak a color or style, update copy/text, add a small utility function, fix a typo in a message.
CRITERIA for change-card: single file or 2-3 files max, hours of work (not days), applies existing patterns, no architecture decisions needed, no new features, self-contained with no cross-feature impact.

TOO LARGE → needs Epic/Feature:
- Requires new architecture or data models
- Touches 4+ files across different layers
- Introduces new user-facing functionality
- Requires multiple phases of work
- Has significant cross-feature dependencies

IF PROPERLY SCOPED AS CHANGE-CARD:
(1) Add validation note: shark change note {{.key}} 'SCOPE_VALIDATED: {reasoning}'
(2) Advance: shark status advance {{.key}}

IF TOO LARGE (should be Epic or Feature):
(1) Document the escalation: shark change note {{.key}} 'ESCALATED: This change-card is too broad. Recommend creating a {Epic/Feature} for: {reason}'
(2) Decline: shark status set {{.key}} declined --note='Scope too broad for change-card — see notes for escalation recommendation'
(3) Report to user: explain what was too large and suggest creating an Epic or Feature instead
